From: rtvdb maintainers
Subject: [rtvdb] Allow Vulkan renderer frame queue depth override

rtvdb requests the surface minimum swapchain image count to avoid the
additional two queued frames used by the SDL default. The build supplies
SDL_VULKAN_FRAME_QUEUE_DEPTH=0 only for the rtvdb Vulkan RT target.

---
 src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c b/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c
index 692dea7db..b37a2de21 100644
--- a/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c
+++ b/src/render/vulkan/SDL_render_vulkan.c
@@ -22,7 +22,9 @@
 
 #ifdef SDL_VIDEO_RENDER_VULKAN
 
+#ifndef SDL_VULKAN_FRAME_QUEUE_DEPTH
 #define SDL_VULKAN_FRAME_QUEUE_DEPTH            2
+#endif
 #define SDL_VULKAN_NUM_VERTEX_BUFFERS           256
 #define SDL_VULKAN_VERTEX_BUFFER_DEFAULT_SIZE   65536
 #define SDL_VULKAN_CONSTANT_BUFFER_DEFAULT_SIZE 65536
